  "question": {
    "text": "What will be the sum of principal and azimuthal quantum number for last electron of Argon?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electronic configuration of<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Ar</mtext><mtext>&nbsp;:&nbsp;</mtext><mn>1</mn><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>,</mtext><mn>2</mn><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mtext>p</mtext><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>,</mtext><mn>3</mn><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mtext>p</mtext><mn>6</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Therefore, quantum numbers for last electron are <math> <mrow> <mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>&amp;</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> so <math> <mrow> <mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow> </math>",
